{"name":"Kidnapper","hex":"#bfc0ab","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"kidnapper","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who kidnaps someone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kidnapper"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kidnapper (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Kidnapper is a 2010 Singaporean thriller film about a kidnap set in Singapore. The first action-thriller film made by Kelvin Tong, it was a joint venture between Scorpio East Pictures of Singapore and RAM Pictures and PMP Entertainment from Malaysia. Tong opted for a thriller film as opposed to a full-fledged action film as he felt this was more realistic in Singapore saying \"people here don't run around with machine guns\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/27/Kidnapper.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kidnapper_(film)","wikidata":"Q6404788"},{"title":"Kidnapper (Blondie song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Kidnapper\" is a song by American rock band Blondie, being released in 1977 as the lead single for the album Plastic Letters in Japan, and as the 11th track of the album in the rest of the world. The song was originally released in 1977 on a Japan-exclusive vinyl single, the song was also later released as an album track in 1978."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kidnapper_(Blondie_song)","wikidata":"Q141659270"},{"title":"Kidnapping","blocks":[{"text":"Kidnapping is the illegal relocation (abduction) and confinement of a person against their will, and is a crime in many jurisdictions. Kidnapping may be accomplished by use of force or fear, or a victim may be enticed into confinement by fraud or deception. Kidnapping is distinguished from false imprisonment by the intentional movement of the victim to a different location."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Dinah_tissot.jpg/330px-Dinah_tissot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kidnapping","wikidata":"Q318296"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/March_2017-_Coors_Kidnapping_Ransom_Note_%2833460504411%29.jpg/500px-March_2017-_Coors_Kidnapping_Ransom_Note_%2833460504411%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/March_2017-_Coors_Kidnapping_Ransom_Note_%2833460504411%29.jpg/500px-March_2017-_Coors_Kidnapping_Ransom_Note_%2833460504411%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMarch_2017-_Coors_Kidnapping_Ransom_Note_(33460504411).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/St%C3%A5hlbergs%27_at_the_railwaystation.jpg/500px-St%C3%A5hlbergs%27_at_the_railwaystation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/St%C3%A5hlbergs%27_at_the_railwaystation.jpg/1280px-St%C3%A5hlbergs%27_at_the_railwaystation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/St%C3%A5hlbergs%27_at_the_railwaystation.jpg/500px-St%C3%A5hlbergs%27_at_the_railwaystation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"K. J. Ståhlberg (in the center-right), the first President of the Republic of Finland, and his wife at the Helsinki Central Station after their kidnapping. Their daughter Elli Ståhlberg stands in the center, behind them.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASt%C3%A5hlbergs'_at_the_railwaystation.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Kidnappers_arrested_Rio.jpg/500px-Kidnappers_arrested_Rio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Kidnappers_arrested_Rio.jpg/500px-Kidnappers_arrested_Rio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Arrested kidnappers in Rio de Janeiro, Brazil lying on the ground","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKidnappers_arrested_Rio.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Kidnappings_Per_100%2C000_Population.png/500px-Kidnappings_Per_100%2C000_Population.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Kidnappings_Per_100%2C000_Population.png/500px-Kidnappings_Per_100%2C000_Population.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The 10 countries with the highest kidnapping rates in 2023[citation needed]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKidnappings_Per_100%2C000_Population.png"}],"sounds":{"kidnapper":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3a/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-kidnapper.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/3a/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-kidnapper.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-kidnapper.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/3a/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-kidnapper.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-kidnapper.wav.ogg"}]}}}